Subject: IR1 Language Runtime And Tooling Decision V1
Date: 2026-05-26
Decision UUID: a098a0e4-91db-4eb9-a4ae-25c0ad2cf70b

@ [slice_surface] docs/slices/IR1_Final_Slices.v1.sop
@ [substrate_boundary] docs/implementation/IR1_Implementation_Substrate_Boundary_And_Invariant_Map.v1.sop
@ [foundation_pack] docs/planning/FSC1_Foundation_Contract_Pack.v1.sop
@ [runtime_graph_pack] docs/planning/FSC3_Runtime_Graph_Proof_Pack.v1.sop
@ [operations_safety_pack] docs/planning/FSC5_Operations_Safety_Pack.v1.sop

& [IR1LanguageRuntimeAndToolingDecisionV1] is the IR1-S02 decision for language runtime and package tooling
  + [decision_id] is ir1-language-runtime-and-tooling-decision-v1
  + [decision_uuid] is a098a0e4-91db-4eb9-a4ae-25c0ad2cf70b
  + [slice_id] is IR1-S02
  + [decision_status] is accepted_by_completion_review_pending
  + [model_route_used] is requires deeper reasoning
  + [implementation_scope] is tooling decision only

  = must: choose tooling that supports SOP authority files, rebuildable SQLite projection, fixture execution, LangGraph integration, and future surface prototypes without elevating generated artifacts to authority
  = must: avoid package installation, code scaffolding, parser implementation, SQLite builder implementation, LangGraph runtime implementation, surface implementation, operations simulator implementation, operations control, and live machine control in this slice

& [SelectedRuntimeStack] is the selected implementation stack for IR1
  + [primary_language] is Python
  + [target_runtime] is Python 3.12 as baseline compatibility target
  + [local_runtime_observed] is Python 3.13.5
  + [runtime_policy] is code should be authored to run on Python 3.12+ unless a later dependency forces a narrower target through completion review
  + [package_metadata_format] is pyproject.toml using PEP 621 project metadata
  + [baseline_package_manager] is python -m venv plus python -m pip
  + [optional_accelerator] is uv may be adopted later by explicit slice if installed or intentionally added
  + [optional_node_role] is Node may support future frontend or tooling surfaces but is not the primary runtime for kernel, parser, projection, or LangGraph work

  = must: keep Python as the substrate for authority parsing, SQLite projection, operator harness, fixture runner, and LangGraph proof runtime unless a future rebake changes the decision
  = must: keep Node out of core authority/runtime implementation until a surface-specific slice authorizes it

& [PackageAndDependencyPolicy] is the package and dependency policy for IR1
  + [dependency_start_state] is no external runtime dependency is required for initial scaffold placeholders
  + [dependency_declaration] is pyproject.toml may declare project metadata before dependencies exist
  + [dependency_addition_rule] is external dependencies may be added only by a slice whose expected output includes dependency declaration or installation
  + [lockfile_policy] is no lockfile is required before external dependencies exist
  + [lockfile_policy] is the first slice that adds external dependencies must define and review the lockfile mechanism
  + [dependency_cache_policy] is dependency caches are generated artifacts and never authority
  + [tool_installation_policy] is this decision does not install tools
  + [uv_policy] is uv is optional and not required because it is not present in the current local environment

  = must: preserve reproducibility through reviewed dependency declaration and completion review, not through hidden local environment state

& [ScriptBoundaryPolicy] is the script boundary for future package metadata
  + [allowed_script_class] is validation command
  + [allowed_script_class] is test command
  + [allowed_script_class] is fixture command
  + [allowed_script_class] is projection rebuild command
  + [allowed_script_class] is format or lint command
  + [forbidden_script_effect] is mutate SOP authority without explicit source-preserving operator
  + [forbidden_script_effect] is treat generated SQLite or cache output as source authority
  + [forbidden_script_effect] is run LangGraph workflow before IR4 authorization
  + [forbidden_script_effect] is open network listener
  + [forbidden_script_effect] is access credentials or secrets
  + [forbidden_script_effect] is launch process or GPU workload
  + [forbidden_script_effect] is dispatch jobs
  + [forbidden_script_effect] is perform destructive filesystem actions

  = must: require every future script to state its authority limit and generated artifact policy before it is trusted

& [LocalDevCommandPolicy] is the local development command policy for future scaffold work
  + [candidate_command] is python -m venv .venv
  + [candidate_command] is python -m pip install -e .[dev]
  + [candidate_command] is python -m pytest
  + [candidate_command] is python -m langsop_cli when a later slice creates an entry point
  + [candidate_command_status] is candidate_only_until_IR1-S05_or_later_authorizes_scaffold_files
  + [command_authority_limit] is local dev commands are convenience projections over accepted source files and tests

  = must: not run package installation or scaffold commands in IR1-S02
  = must: review local command effects before any future slice uses them as verification

& [ToolingInvalidationConditionSet] is the invalidation set for this tooling decision
  + [invalidated_by] is change to IR1-S01 substrate boundary
  + [invalidated_by] is accepted dependency requiring runtime unsupported by Python 3.12+
  + [invalidated_by] is LangGraph integration proof requiring a different runtime boundary
  + [invalidated_by] is multi-user surface implementation requiring a separate frontend package boundary
  + [invalidated_by] is generated artifact policy contradiction
  + [invalidated_by] is package tooling creating hidden authority state
  + [invalidated_by] is operations control or live machine control leak

  = must: rerun IR1-S02 review if any invalidation condition is found

& [IR1S02CoverageReview] is the coverage checklist for IR1-S02
  + [selected_runtime_stack_present] is SelectedRuntimeStack
  + [package_dependency_policy_present] is PackageAndDependencyPolicy
  + [script_boundary_policy_present] is ScriptBoundaryPolicy
  + [local_dev_command_policy_present] is LocalDevCommandPolicy
  + [tooling_invalidation_conditions_present] is ToolingInvalidationConditionSet
  + [python_runtime_selected] is true
  + [pyproject_metadata_selected] is true
  + [baseline_package_manager_selected] is python -m venv plus python -m pip
  + [package_installation_performed] is false
  + [code_scaffold_created] is false
  + [forbidden_scope_absent] is package installation
  + [forbidden_scope_absent] is code scaffolding
  + [forbidden_scope_absent] is parser implementation
  + [forbidden_scope_absent] is SQLite builder implementation
  + [forbidden_scope_absent] is LangGraph implementation
  + [forbidden_scope_absent] is surface implementation
  + [forbidden_scope_absent] is adapter implementation
  + [forbidden_scope_absent] is operations simulator implementation
  + [forbidden_scope_absent] is operations control
  + [forbidden_scope_absent] is live machine control

  = must: open IR1-S03 only after this decision is accepted by completion review
